As an operator, you'll work in a two-shift system and be responsible for part of the production process. By operating the machines, your goal is to meet production demand with the desired quality. Independently operate, monitor, and maintain the production line;

- Identify and resolve machine malfunctions;
- Set up machines based on the production schedule;
- Monitor product quality using various measuring instruments;
- Ensure timely machine maintenance in consultation with your manager and the Technical Department;
- Contribute to structural improvement opportunities;
- Coordinating workflows in consultation with your manager.

- A technical background or extensive experience in production technology is a plus;
- You are willing to work night shifts;
- You have technical knowledge and enjoy brainstorming;
- You are a natural at solution-oriented error analysis;
- You are a precision engineer;
- You have knowledge of and experience with production processes;
- You are decisive, practical, and enjoy working in a team.
- A driving license (car) is preferred - Maintec arranges transport;
- You can communicate in English at a B1/B2 level.

Wat ga je precies doen
As an Assistant Warehouse Manager, you’re right at the heart of our warehouse operations in Tilburg. You keep an eye on daily performance, coordinate activities on the floor and use data to find smarter ways of working. From improving processes to managing costs, your work has a direct impact on the success of the warehouse.
What You Will Do:
- Coordinate: supply chain processes and manage relationships with suppliers to ensure smooth operations;
- Monitor: costs and review invoices to identify and implement cost-saving opportunities;
- Analyze: performance metrics and prepare reports (e.g., WBR and MBR) to improve KPI outcomes;
- Oversee: workforce planning, including managing temporary staff to meet operational demands;
- Support: operational tasks and act as the point of contact for internal departments like Finance and Accounting.



Wat bieden we jou
Your development matters to us. Along with strong employment benefits, you’ll get opportunities to learn, grow and take the next steps in your career. Here’s what we offer:
- Monthly salary between €2,700 and €3,500;
- Permanent contract upon successful completion of probation;
- Full-time position of 40 hours per week;
- 8% holiday allowance on top of your salary;
- Attractive pension plan for your future security;
- Ample room for initiative and independence.




Functie-eisen
We’re looking for a proactive problem-solver who enjoys working with data, improving processes and making warehouse operations run more efficiently.
- 5+ years of experience in warehousing;
- MBO+ education or demonstrable HBO-level thinking and working skills;
- Proficient in MS Office, especially Excel;
- Fluent in English; Dutch or other languages are a plus;
- Strong numerical analysis skills; proactive and solution-oriented.



